<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#aboutElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-07, SA-11, SA-13, SA-23. One element per assertion; a later assertion about the same operator and element is a recheck."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#aboutElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "about element"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#aboutElement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The situation element that a perception assertion says the operator perceived."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptationCarriedFrom
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptationCarriedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptationCarriedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptationCarriedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptationCarriedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptationCarriedFrom> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HA24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptationCarriedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-14. Used when a mode change starts a new engagement over the same link, or when the operator drives the same setup again, so that the adaptation built up over earlier drives (HA24) is not lost. The earlier engagement has the same operator and started before this one (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl); with ROVO-link loaded, both must use the same teleoperation setup (ROVO-link-shapes.ttl). Whether an adaptation is still valid after a long pause is decided by the stream layer, which then gives no value."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptationCarriedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "adaptation carried from"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptationCarriedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The earlier engagement of the same operator whose adapted information age this engagement continues with."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptedInformationAge
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptedInformationAge> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptedInformationAge> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptedInformationAge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptedInformationAge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dayTimeDuration> .
<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dayTimeDuration> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToMode
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-09, SA-12, SA-14, SA-18, SA-24. A limit stated for a broader mode (ROVO-op:broaderMode) holds for its narrower modes unless they have their own. Not used on an SARequirement, which is scoped by SA type (forSAType)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "applies to mode"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToMode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An operation mode in which a configured limit applies."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#assertedOperator
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#assertedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#assertedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#assertedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#assertedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#assertedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-07. Where the assertion rests on a displayed scene, this is the operator of an engagement the scene was shown in (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#assertedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "asserted operator"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#assertedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The remote operator whose perception a perception assertion estimates."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#availableChannel
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#availableChannel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#availableChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#availableChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#availableChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-15, SA-16, SA-17: the channels the station currently provides to the operator for the engaged vehicle."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#availableChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "available channel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#availableChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An information channel the remote station currently provides to the operator in an engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#basedOnScene
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#basedOnScene> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#basedOnScene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#basedOnScene> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#basedOnScene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#basedOnScene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#basedOnScene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The displayed scene the operator perceived the element in; through it, when the information was sensed at the vehicle (SA-11)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#basedOnScene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "based on scene"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#basedOnScene> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The displayed scene in which the operator perceived the element."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#broaderMode
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#broaderMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#broaderMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#broaderMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#broaderMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#broaderMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01 and every question that reads a limit per mode. Continuous and event-based remote driving have ROVO-op:RemoteDriving as their broader mode. Limits, supported modes, task kinds and needs stated for a broader mode hold for its narrower modes. A property of this module, not skos:broader, so that the SKOS mappings of ROVO-core add nothing to the mode hierarchy."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#broaderMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "broader mode"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#broaderMode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The more general operation mode that an operation mode is a special case of."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#captureDelay
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#captureDelay> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#captureDelay> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#captureDelay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#captureDelay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dayTimeDuration> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#concernsElement
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#concernsElement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#concernsElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#concernsElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SituationElement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#concernsElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03, SA-13, SA-22, SA-23. Optional, and a request can name several. For decision-support SA, the requirements then apply only to these elements, not to every element of the required type in the vehicle's scene; a request that names none is judged on every element of the type."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#concernsElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "concerns element"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#concernsElement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A situation element that a request is about, e.g. the object the vehicle cannot classify."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#deployedIn
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#deployedIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#deployedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#deployedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#deployedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-06, static: the environments the vehicle is deployed in."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#deployedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "deployed in"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#deployedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A kind of place the vehicle is deployed in."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#derivedFromFrame
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#derivedFromFrame> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#derivedFromFrame> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#derivedFromFrame> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFrame> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#derivedFromFrame> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-08: a sensor frame the displayed scene was produced from. Not a subproperty of prov:wasDerivedFrom: that would type a SensorFrame as a prov:Entity, while a sosa:Observation is a prov:Activity in the SSN-PROV alignment, and the two are disjoint."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#derivedFromFrame> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "derived from frame"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#derivedFromFrame> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A sensor frame that a displayed scene was produced from."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedOperator
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasAssociatedWith> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01, SA-05. An engagement has exactly one; the vehicles an operator is responsible for at the same time are those of the operator's open engagements."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "engaged operator"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The remote operator who is responsible for the vehicle in an engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedVehicle
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01. An engagement has exactly one, and a vehicle has at most one open engagement at a time (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "engaged vehicle"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The vehicle that the operator monitors, assists or drives in an engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementEnvironment
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-06, runtime. A vehicle can be deployed in several environments (deployedIn), so the answer for one engagement is stated here. It must be one of the vehicle's environments where the vehicle states any (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl). Without a value, SA-06 has an answer only if the vehicle states exactly one environment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "engagement environment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The operating environment the vehicle is in during this engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DrivingTask> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-06, runtime. As engagementEnvironment: one of the vehicle's driving tasks where the vehicle states any. Without a value, SA-06 has an answer only if the vehicle states exactly one driving task."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "engagement task"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#engagementTask> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The driving task the vehicle is operated for during this engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#followsEngagement
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#followsEngagement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#followsEngagement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasInformedBy> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#followsEngagement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#followsEngagement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#followsEngagement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#followsEngagement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-04. The operator moves on from an engagement already held: usually into another mode, e.g. from remote monitoring into event-based remote driving, on the operator's own initiative or on a request from the vehicle (the engagement then also has respondsTo); or in the same mode, when a reconnection in a new session starts a new engagement. The build-up then starts from the SA already held, not from zero: a perception assertion belongs to the operator, not to one engagement, so what the operator perceived in the earlier engagement still counts while it is within its recheck interval (SA-23). SA-04 names the engagement followed. The earlier engagement has ended and has the same operator and vehicle (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#followsEngagement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "follows engagement"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#followsEngagement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The engagement of the same operator with the same vehicle that this engagement directly continues from."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forDrivingTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DrivingTask> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forDrivingTask> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-22. Optional: the requirement applies only to engagements with this driving task (engagementTask, or the vehicle's only driving task), e.g. the fork and the load in pallet handling (WO25). Without it, the requirement applies to every driving task."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "for driving task"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The driving task to which an SA requirement is limited."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forEnvironment
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forEnvironment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HN25b" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forEnvironment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-22. Optional: the requirement applies only to engagements in this operating environment (engagementEnvironment, or the vehicle's only environment). Without it, the requirement applies in every environment. Which elements matter depends on where and for what the vehicle is operated (WO25, HN25b)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "for environment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The operating environment to which an SA requirement is limited."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forRequestType
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-22. Optional, for decision-support SA: the requirement applies only while the operator answers a request of this type. Without it, the requirement applies to every request."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "for request type"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The request type to which an SA requirement for decision-support SA is limited."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forSAType
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forSAType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forSAType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forSAType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forSAType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forSAType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-22. The requirement applies to engagements in a mode that requires this SA type (requiresSAType)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forSAType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "for SA type"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#forSAType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The SA type that an SA requirement belongs to."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasDrivingTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DrivingTask> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-06, static: the driving tasks the vehicle is deployed for."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has driving task"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasDrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A purpose the vehicle is deployed for."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestReason
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestReason> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. A request can have several reasons; one without a stated cause has ROVO-op:UnspecifiedReason."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has request reason"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestReason> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reason given for a request."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestType
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03, SA-22. A takeover request starts event-based remote driving, any other type remote assistance; for decision-support SA the type selects the required elements (forRequestType)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has request type"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasRequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "What a request asks the remote operator for: a takeover or a kind of assistance."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#holdsTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#holdsTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#holdsTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#holdsTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#holdsTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-02, runtime: the tasks the operator holds in this engagement. Objects are task individuals typed with a task class (an EDMC DDT subtask class or one of the classes above)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#holdsTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "holds task"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#holdsTask> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A task the operator holds for the vehicle in an engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inOperationMode
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inOperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inOperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inOperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inOperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inOperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01. An engagement uses one specific mode: not the broad remote driving mode."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inOperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "in operation mode"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inOperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The operation mode an engagement is in."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inSceneOf
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inSceneOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inSceneOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SituationElement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inSceneOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inSceneOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Interface (scene and criticality module): the element is currently relevant to the vehicle's situation. SA-13 and SA-23 apply the requirements to these elements."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inSceneOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "in scene of"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inSceneOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The vehicle whose current situation a situation element is relevant to."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#modeIncludesTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#modeIncludesTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#modeIncludesTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#modeIncludesTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-02, static: which kinds of task a mode gives the operator. The object is a task class IRI (OWL 2 punning), e.g. vla:LateralVehicleMotionControl or ROVO-op:DecisionMakingTask. It lists the kinds a mode may give the operator, not the tasks every engagement in the mode holds. A task stated for a broader mode holds for its narrower modes (broaderMode). The tasks of remote monitoring and remote assistance are asserted below; those of remote driving are EDMC classes and are asserted in ROVO-core.ttl."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#modeIncludesTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mode includes task"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#modeIncludesTask> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A kind of task that an operation mode gives the operator, stated as a task class."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onChannel
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onChannel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-08. E.g. the camera view a scene appeared in. Recorded with the scene."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "on channel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An information channel on which a displayed scene was shown."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#providesCue
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#providesCue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#providesCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#providesCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Cue> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#providesCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-16. Asserted per channel individual, because what a channel conveys depends on the station."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#providesCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "provides cue"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#providesCue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A cue that an information channel conveys to the operator."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#readyOperator
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#readyOperator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#readyOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasAssociatedWith> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#readyOperator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#readyOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#FallbackReadyPeriod> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#readyOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#readyOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-20. The same operator has no engagement during the period (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#readyOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ready operator"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#readyOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The remote operator who is fallback-ready during a fallback-ready period."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requestedBy
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. The engagement that responds to the request is with this vehicle (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "requested by"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requestedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The vehicle that issued a request."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresElementType
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresElementType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresElementType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresElementType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresElementType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-22. The object is a class IRI, e.g. an A.U.T.O. class such as l4:Pedestrian (OWL 2 punning)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresElementType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "requires element type"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresElementType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The type of situation element, stated as a class, that an SA requirement says the operator must have perceived."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-21: each mode requires one SA type."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "requires SA type"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The SA type an operator needs in order to work in an operation mode."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#respondsTo
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#respondsTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#respondsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#used> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#respondsTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#respondsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#respondsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#respondsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. The request that started an engagement: a takeover request for event-based remote driving, an assistance request for remote assistance. Continuous remote driving and remote monitoring engagements respond to none; an event-based engagement that the operator started without a request, from remote monitoring or from an on-board driver, responds to none either. For a takeover from an on-board driver, SA-03 is then answered by the takeover reason (takeoverReason)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#respondsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "responds to"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#respondsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The request from the vehicle that an engagement was started to answer."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#rulesOutMode
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#rulesOutMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#rulesOutMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#rulesOutMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#rulesOutMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-24. Configuration: while the operator's latest ImpairmentObservation for the impairment is true, the modes named here drop out of the answer to SA-24. A mode stated here also rules out its narrower modes (ROVO-op:broaderMode). No values are asserted by this module: no source says which impairment rules out which mode, so an impairment without a value rules out none."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#rulesOutMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "rules out mode"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#rulesOutMode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A mode that an operator who currently shows signs of this impairment cannot perform."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensorOfVehicle
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensorOfVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensorOfVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensorOfVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensorOfVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensorOfVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-08. Interface (vehicle state). Ties a sensor frame, through its sensor, to a vehicle: the frames of a displayed scene come from the vehicle of an engagement the scene was shown in, where their sensors state a vehicle (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensorOfVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sensor of vehicle"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensorOfVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The vehicle that a sensor is mounted on."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#shownIn
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#shownIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#shownIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#shownIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#shownIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-08, SA-09. Ties a scene to the operator, the vehicle and the mode whose information age limit applies to it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#shownIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "shown in"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#shownIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An engagement during which a displayed scene was shown to the operator."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportedBy
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-25. Every perception assertion has at least one, since perception is never asserted as fact."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "supported by"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A piece of SA evidence from which a perception assertion was inferred."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportsMode
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportsMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportsMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportsMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportsMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Interface (ROVO-concept). The modes the vehicle's equipment allows (SA-24). A vehicle without an ADS does not support remote assistance; it can support remote monitoring, continuous remote driving, and event-based remote driving where it can be taken over from an on-board driver. Support stated for a broader mode holds for its narrower modes (ROVO-op:broaderMode): a vehicle that supports ROVO-op:RemoteDriving supports both remote driving contexts. Support stated for a narrower mode holds for that mode only."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportsMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "supports mode"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#supportsMode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An operation mode that the vehicle's equipment allows it to be operated in."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takenOverFrom
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takenOverFrom> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takenOverFrom> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takenOverFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takenOverFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriver> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takenOverFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01, LK-10. A record of the takeover, which stays when the driver can no longer drive; whether control can go back to the driver (ROVO-link:HandBackToOnBoardDriver) is stated with ableToTakeOver. Only on event-based remote driving engagements (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takenOverFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "taken over from"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takenOverFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The on-board driver from whom an event-based remote driving engagement took over."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takeoverReason
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takeoverReason> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takeoverReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takeoverReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverReason> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takeoverReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. Only on an engagement that took over from an on-board driver (takenOverFrom), which responds to no request (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl). Optional, and an engagement can state several."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takeoverReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "takeover reason"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#takeoverReason> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reason why the operator took over from the on-board driver in an engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viaChannel
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viaChannel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viaChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viaChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viaChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-07: the channel the element was perceived through."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viaChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "via channel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viaChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An information channel through which the operator perceived the element."@en .
