# http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/resultTime
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/resultTime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/resultTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ableToTakeOver
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ableToTakeOver> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ableToTakeOver> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ableToTakeOver> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriver> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ableToTakeOver> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ableToTakeOver> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "LK-10. Interface (driver monitoring, vehicle state). True while the driver is on board and fit to drive; false when the driver cannot drive, e.g. after a takeover with the reason ROVO-op:OnBoardDriverUnableToDrive. Absent means not known, and then handing control back to the driver does not count as available (ROVO-link:OnBoardDriverCanTakeOver)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ableToTakeOver> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "able to take over"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ableToTakeOver> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Whether an on-board driver is able to take control of the vehicle back now."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptedInformationAge
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#adaptedInformationAge> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToFallbackReady
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToFallbackReady> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToFallbackReady> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToFallbackReady> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToFallbackReady> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToFallbackReady> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-18. True for a limit that applies while the operator is fallback-ready rather than in a mode."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToFallbackReady> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "applies to fallback-ready"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#appliesToFallbackReady> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Whether a configured limit applies while the operator is fallback-ready, a state that has no operation mode."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "LU17" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MZ25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-04. Set by the stream layer from SA-23; absent while build-up lasts. Build-up time = buildUpEndedAt minus prov:startedAtTime. Basic scene content is perceived within a single fixation (MZ25); from video, a traffic scene's layout can be reproduced after about 7-12 s, while relative speeds take 20 s or more (LU17)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "build-up ended at"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#buildUpEndedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "When the operator's SA was first sufficient for the SA type of the engagement's mode (SA-23), which ends the build-up phase and starts the maintenance phase."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#captureDelay
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#captureDelay> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#confidence
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#confidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#confidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#confidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#confidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#confidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-13, SA-23, SA-25. How the estimator combines evidence is outside the ontology. Whether an assertion counts as perceived is decided against the PerceptionConfidenceThreshold of the mode."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#confidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "confidence"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#confidence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "How sure the estimate is that the operator perceived the element, between 0 (not at all) and 1 (certain)."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#displayedAt
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#displayedAt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#displayedAt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#displayedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#displayedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#displayedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-09. Information age = displayedAt minus the earliest sensed time (capture time minus capture delay) of the frames the scene was derived from."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#displayedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "displayed at"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#displayedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The time at which the remote station showed a displayed scene to the operator."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasADS
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasADS> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasADS> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasADS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasADS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasADS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Interface (ROVO-concept). SA-24, LK-10. True for an ADS-equipped vehicle, false for a vehicle without an ADS; absent means not known, never 'no ADS'. A vehicle with hasADS false does not support remote assistance, is driven in event-based remote driving only when taken over from an on-board driver (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl), and has no ROVO-link:adsWithinODD value. Separates 'no ADS' from 'ADS outside its ODD', which ROVO-link:adsWithinODD alone cannot."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasADS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has ADS"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#hasADS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Whether the vehicle is equipped with an automated driving system."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#horizontalFieldOfView
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#horizontalFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#horizontalFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#horizontalFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CameraView> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#horizontalFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#horizontalFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-17. The horizontal angle a camera view shows, in degrees. Camera views of one engagement are assumed not to overlap; overlapping cameras are declared as one stitched view with its combined angle."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#horizontalFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "horizontal field of view"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#horizontalFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The horizontal angle that a camera view shows, in degrees."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HA24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-17. Configuration: the required field, e.g. a licence minimum, not the wider field a driver may actually have. AM22 gives driving-licence minimums of 120 degrees for cars and 160 degrees for trucks and buses, so camera arrays should cover at least that. The in-vehicle field is centred on the vehicle's forward axis: from minus half this value to plus half of it. Coverage = the part of that field, in degrees, that the available camera views show (each view's interval from viewDirection and horizontalFieldOfView, clipped to the in-vehicle field, summed), divided by this value. It is a share between 0 and 1: views outside the in-vehicle field, such as a rear camera, add nothing to it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "in-vehicle field of view"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#inVehicleFieldOfView> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The horizontal visual field, in degrees, that a driver seated in the vehicle must have, taken as the reference for the operator's camera views."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-12, SA-24, LK-10. Lets SA-24 order modes without ROVO-concept. It repeats what ROVO-op:broaderMode ROVO-op:RemoteDriving already says, so the shapes check that the two agree (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl, OperationModeShape)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is remote driving mode"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Whether an operation mode is remote driving or one of its narrower modes, in which the operator holds vehicle motion control."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#lowerBound
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#lowerBound> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#lowerBound> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#lowerBound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#lowerBound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#lowerBound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-18. A workload estimate below it is underload. MU21 and ME24 describe underload and decreased vigilance in operators who wait or have little to do."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#lowerBound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "lower bound"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#lowerBound> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The lowest workload value, on the band's scale, that still counts as acceptable."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onScale
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onScale> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onScale> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onScale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onScale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-18. A band applies only to estimates on the same scale. Used on WorkloadEstimate and WorkloadBand, so no domain is declared (a domain would need a union, which OWL 2 RL does not allow)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onScale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "on scale"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#onScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The name of the scale on which a workload estimate or a workload band is expressed."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#perceivedAt
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#perceivedAt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#perceivedAt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#perceivedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#perceivedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#perceivedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-07, SA-13, SA-23. Not the capture or display time."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#perceivedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "perceived at"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#perceivedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The time at which the operator perceived the element, e.g. the time of the fixation."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#reliability
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#reliability> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#reliability> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#reliability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#reliability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#reliability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Between 0 and 1 (SA-25)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#reliability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reliability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#reliability> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "How far a piece of SA evidence can be trusted as a sign that the operator perceived the element, between 0 and 1."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensedAt
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensedAt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensedAt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-07, SA-11, SA-23. For perception through a channel that shows no scene built from sensor frames, such as audio or haptic feedback. The sensed time of a perception assertion is: the earliest sensed time of the frames of its scene (basedOnScene); otherwise this value; otherwise perceivedAt, i.e. no delay is assumed, which the shapes report as a warning. The assertion is stale when its element changed after that time (ElementStateChange). Not used together with basedOnScene."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sensed at"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#sensedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "When the information the operator perceived was sensed at the vehicle, for a perception that rests on no displayed scene."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#upperBound
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#upperBound> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#upperBound> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#upperBound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#upperBound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#upperBound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-18. A workload estimate above it is overload."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#upperBound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "upper bound"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#upperBound> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The highest workload value, on the band's scale, that still counts as acceptable."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viewDirection
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viewDirection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viewDirection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viewDirection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CameraView> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viewDirection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viewDirection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-17. With horizontalFieldOfView it gives the angular interval the view shows: from viewDirection minus half the field of view to viewDirection plus half of it. An interval that passes 180 or -180 continues on the other side: a view centred at 170 with a field of view of 60 shows 140 to 180 and -180 to -160. A camera view without a value is taken as centred straight ahead (0)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viewDirection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "view direction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#viewDirection> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The direction of the centre of a camera view, in degrees clockwise from the vehicle's forward axis, from -180 to 180 (0 = straight ahead, 90 = right, 180 = rear)."@en .
