# http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> .
# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> .
# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ActuatorLatencyLimit
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ActuatorLatencyLimit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ActuatorLatencyLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ActuatorLatencyLimit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "GF20" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ActuatorLatencyLimit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MA25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ActuatorLatencyLimit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TANG26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ActuatorLatencyLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-24: a mode whose limit the current actuator latency exceeds is one the operator can no longer perform. The operator-side counterpart of InformationAgeLimit for the other latency part. The value compared with it is the latest ROVO-link:ActuatorLatency observation of the session that carries the engagement, so it needs ROVO-link. A setup's reference budgets for the actuator latency (ROVO-link:LatencyBudget) hold up to a vehicle speed and are checked separately, by LK-04; SA-24 uses this limit only. A configuration parameter; GF20 and MA25 give measured values, not limits."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ActuatorLatencyLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "actuator latency limit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ActuatorLatencyLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The largest actuator latency, from the operator's input to the actuator response at the vehicle, that the operator can be expected to anticipate in a mode. Value as qudt:numericValue with qudt:unit unit:MilliSEC."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AudioChannel
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AudioChannel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AudioChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AudioChannel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AudioChannel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AudioChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-15. WO25: all six operators named missing audio as a major issue for SA."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AudioChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "audio channel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AudioChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Sound from the vehicle and its surroundings, relayed to the operator."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CameraView
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CameraView> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CameraView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CameraView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-15, SA-17."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CameraView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "camera view"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CameraView> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An information channel that shows the operator the image of one vehicle camera, or one image stitched from several."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-09, SA-12, SA-14, SA-18, SA-22 and SA-24, and the limits of ROVO-link. Limits are parameters, not facts about the world. Most limit types hold one value in one fixed unit, given in the definition, as qudt:numericValue with qudt:unit; the shapes enforce the unit, and queries read only that unit. Two differ: a WorkloadBand has a lower and an upper bound on a named scale, and a ROVO-link:TravelTolerance can be given as a dimensionless delay limit. Most limits are scoped by mode (appliesToMode); an SARequirement is scoped by SA type and its value is the recheck interval. Every limit carries dct:source; values used for testing say so in rdfs:comment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "configured limit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A value set by configuration that a measured or computed quantity is compared with, together with the source it was taken from."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ControlInputEvidence
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ControlInputEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ControlInputEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ControlInputEvidence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MZ25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ControlInputEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-25."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ControlInputEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "control input evidence"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ControlInputEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "SA evidence from a control action of the operator that implies the element was perceived, e.g. braking for a pedestrian."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Cue
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Cue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Cue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-16."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Cue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "cue"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Cue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A kind of sensory information a driver uses, such as vestibular or auditory information."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CueInterpretationTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CueInterpretationTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CueInterpretationTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionMakingTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionMakingTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionMakingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-08. Separates the scene the operator sees from the current scene at the vehicle."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "displayed scene"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DisplayedScene> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "What the remote station showed the operator at one moment, derived from one or more sensor frames."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DrivingTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DrivingTask> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HN25b" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DrivingTask> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-06. Not the DDT (which every driving task needs) but the purpose of the operation; where J3016's driving task is meant, R.O.V.O writes DDT. Not an OperatorTask either, which is what the operator does (holdsTask), while engagementTask and ROVO-link:setupTask name a driving task. It shapes which elements matter (WO25: fork handling). Individuals are configuration."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "driving task"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DrivingTask> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "What the vehicle is operated for, e.g. passenger transport, pallet handling or vehicle relocation."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ElementStateChange
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ElementStateChange> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ElementStateChange> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ElementStateChange> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ElementStateChange> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-11. Interface (stream layer): sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest is the element and sosa:resultTime the time. A perception assertion is stale when its element changed after the sensed time of the scene it rests on. What counts as significant is decided upstream."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ElementStateChange> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "element state change"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ElementStateChange> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An observation, made at the vehicle, that a situation element's state changed significantly, e.g. a pedestrian started crossing."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01, SA-04, SA-05. An engagement is not a session: a session (ROVO-link:TeleoperationSession) is only the connection between a station and a vehicle, and carries engagements in sequence. An engagement is carried by one session and ends with it, so a reconnection in a new session also starts a new engagement, in the same mode; it can name the one it continues (followsEngagement). What sources such as HA24 call a driving session is an engagement here."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "engagement"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Engagement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The period in which one remote operator is responsible for one vehicle in one operation mode, from prov:startedAtTime to prov:endedAtTime (absent while it lasts). A mode change starts a new engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EyeFixationEvidence
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EyeFixationEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EyeFixationEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EyeFixationEvidence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MZ25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EyeFixationEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-25."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EyeFixationEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "eye fixation evidence"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EyeFixationEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "SA evidence that the operator's gaze rested on the element in the displayed scene."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#FallbackReadyPeriod
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#FallbackReadyPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#FallbackReadyPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#FallbackReadyPeriod> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EN95a" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#FallbackReadyPeriod> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#FallbackReadyPeriod> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#FallbackReadyPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-20. An operator state, not an operation mode: there is no vehicle and no mode. Waiting can bring underload and decreased vigilance (MU21, ME24, EN95a). Counts as a break for SA-12. Not J3016's DDT fallback-ready user, who is the user of one vehicle with an engaged Level 3 ADS and is receptive to its requests to intervene: an operator who waits for the requests of one vehicle while watching it is in remote monitoring here, and this state has no vehicle (related match in ROVO-core)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#FallbackReadyPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fallback-ready period"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#FallbackReadyPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A period in which an operator waits, ready to take over, without being engaged with a vehicle, from prov:startedAtTime to prov:endedAtTime (absent while it lasts)."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#HapticFeedback
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#HapticFeedback> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#HapticFeedback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#HapticFeedback> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#HapticFeedback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-15, SA-16. TL22 reports the missing haptic channel as a problem for remote operators."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#HapticFeedback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "haptic feedback"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#HapticFeedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Force or touch feedback to the operator, e.g. steering-wheel torque or pedal feel."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HA24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-19."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "impairment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A kind of operator impairment that operator monitoring can show signs of."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ImpairmentObservation
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ImpairmentObservation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ImpairmentObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ImpairmentObservation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HA24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ImpairmentObservation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ImpairmentObservation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ImpairmentObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-19, SA-20, SA-24. How the monitoring decides is outside the ontology (e.g. a distraction or drowsiness monitor)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ImpairmentObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "impairment observation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ImpairmentObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An observation by operator monitoring of whether the operator shows signs of an impairment: sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest the operator, sosa:observedProperty the impairment, sosa:hasSimpleResult true or false, sosa:resultTime the time."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Cue> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "LV21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-16: missing cues are the in-vehicle cues that no available channel provides. The individuals are the examples SA-16 lists; not an exhaustive list."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "in-vehicle cue"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A cue an in-vehicle driver would normally have."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationAgeLimit
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationAgeLimit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationAgeLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationAgeLimit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationAgeLimit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "GF20" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationAgeLimit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationAgeLimit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "NE19" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationAgeLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-09. The limit per mode is the operator-side limit and takes priority. ROVO-link may scope a further instance to a teleoperation setup (ROVO-link:appliesToSetup) as the vehicle-to-station part of the setup's reference budgets (LK-04); it must be no looser than the mode's limit, which the link shapes check. With ROVO-link loaded, SA-09 uses the setup's limit where it is stricter. SA-24: a mode whose limit the current information age exceeds is one the operator can no longer perform; each candidate mode is tested against its own limit. Without a displayed scene, or for a mode without a limit, the information age is not judged and rules out no mode."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationAgeLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "information age limit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationAgeLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The largest event-to-display age of displayed information acceptable in a mode. Value as qudt:numericValue with qudt:unit unit:MilliSEC."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "LV21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-15. Channel individuals belong to a station; what each conveys is asserted per individual (providesCue)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "information channel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A means by which the remote station conveys information about the vehicle and its surroundings to the operator."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#LatencyChangeLimit
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#LatencyChangeLimit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#LatencyChangeLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#LatencyChangeLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-14. A configuration parameter; no published value."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#LatencyChangeLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "latency change limit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#LatencyChangeLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The largest difference between the current and the adapted information age acceptable in a mode before the operator's adaptation can no longer be assumed. Value as qudt:numericValue with qudt:unit unit:MilliSEC."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MapView
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MapView> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MapView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MapView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-15."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MapView> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "map view"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MapView> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An information channel that shows the vehicle's position and route on a map or in a bird's-eye view."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MinimumBreakLength
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MinimumBreakLength> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MinimumBreakLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MinimumBreakLength> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HA24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MinimumBreakLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-12. A break itself has no mode; the mode named here (appliesToMode) is the remote driving mode whose time on task the break resets, see TimeOnTaskLimit for the rules. HA24: most drivers reported breaks of 10-15 min once per hour."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MinimumBreakLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "minimum break length"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MinimumBreakLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The shortest time without an engagement that counts as a break for the time-on-task limit of a remote driving mode. Value as qudt:numericValue with qudt:unit unit:MIN."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionFeedback
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionFeedback> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionFeedback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionFeedback> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionFeedback> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionFeedback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-15. Motion platforms were tested in WO26 and WO25."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionFeedback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "motion feedback"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionFeedback> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Feedback that lets the operator feel the vehicle's motion, e.g. through a motion platform."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObservationTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObservationTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObservationTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriver
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriver> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriver> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriver> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "J3016" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriver> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01, LK-10. Close to EDMC InVehicleDriver (ROVO-core); a SKOS mapping, since the on-board driver does not drive while a remote operator has taken over. Whether the driver can take control back is a separate state (ableToTakeOver)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriver> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "on-board driver"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriver> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A human in the vehicle's driver's seat who drives the vehicle when no remote operator does."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "BR26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HN25b" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "LV21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-06. Interface (ROVO-todd): the teleoperation ODD describes environments by their attributes; these individuals only name the kind. The environment matters for remote driving: performance and training differ per ODD (HN25b), and a monotonous task reduces SA (LV21)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "operating environment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The kind of place a vehicle is operated in, e.g. a public road, a warehouse, a port, or a construction or mining site."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "BSI1886" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01, SA-21. The modes of AM22 (remote monitoring, remote assistance, remote driving), with remote driving split into its two contexts by ROVO-op:broaderMode. Fallback-ready is not a mode but an operator state (FallbackReadyPeriod). Interface (ROVO-concept)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "operation mode"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The kind of remote operation an engagement performs."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "J3016" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-02. In remote driving, DDT subtasks and the DDT fallback: EDMC's DynamicDrivingSubtask and DynamicDrivingTaskFallback are subclasses (ROVO-core). In remote assistance, decision-making and cue interpretation, e.g. classifying an object or authorizing a path; the remote assistant 'only provides input and authorization' without performing any part of the DDT (AM22). In remote monitoring, observation only."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "operator task"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatorTask> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A task a remote operator can hold for a vehicle in an engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EN95a" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MZ25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-07, SA-11, SA-25. Carries no SA level: comprehension and projection integrate several elements and are not held per element. A later assertion about the same operator and element is a recheck (SA-13)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "perception assertion"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An estimate, produced from evidence, that an operator perceived a given situation element at a given time, in a displayed scene or through a channel that shows none, such as audio."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionConfidenceThreshold
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionConfidenceThreshold> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionConfidenceThreshold> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionConfidenceThreshold> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-13, SA-23. An assertion below the threshold of the mode of the engagement whose SA is judged does not count as perceived or as a recheck. Where no threshold is configured for the mode or a broader mode, every assertion counts. A configuration parameter; no source gives a value."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionConfidenceThreshold> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "perception confidence threshold"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionConfidenceThreshold> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The lowest confidence at which a perception assertion counts as the operator having perceived the element, in a mode. Value as qudt:numericValue between 0 and 1 with qudt:unit unit:UNITLESS."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ProbeAnswerEvidence
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ProbeAnswerEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ProbeAnswerEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ProbeAnswerEvidence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EN95b" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ProbeAnswerEvidence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MZ25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ProbeAnswerEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-25."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ProbeAnswerEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "probe answer evidence"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ProbeAnswerEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "SA evidence from the operator's answer to a query about the situation that is put during the task, as in SAGAT or SPAM."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "J3016" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "SHI26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01. EDMC RemoteDriver and RemoteAssistant are subclasses (ROVO-core). The station is usually outside the vehicle, but J3016 (definition 3.31.1.2) also counts a remote driver inside the vehicle who is not in the driver's seat; cues such a driver perceives directly, not through the station, are not modelled (SHI26 note this case)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "remote operator"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A human who monitors, assists or drives a vehicle through a remote station, without occupying the vehicle's driver's seat."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01, SA-24. Interface. Related to EDMC MotorVehicle by a SKOS mapping (ROVO-core), not a subclass: vehicles off public roads, such as forklifts, are included. Whether it has an ADS is stated with hasADS."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "remotely operated vehicle"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemotelyOperatedVehicle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A vehicle that can be monitored, assisted or driven from a remote station. It may or may not have an automated driving system."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. Issued by the vehicle's ADS. A takeover from an on-board driver responds to no request; why it happened is recorded on the engagement (takeoverReason). A takeover request closely matches J3016's request to intervene (ROVO-core). For decision-support SA, the request type and the elements the request concerns select the required elements (SA-22, concernsElement)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "request"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Request> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A request from a vehicle to a remote operator: to take over (event-based remote driving) or to assist (remote assistance), with an issue time (prov:generatedAtTime)."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. Sensor failure and perception error (MU21, citing California DMV 2019), plan failure (MU21, citing Scholtz et al. 2004), an object the vehicle cannot classify (AM22), and no stated cause. Not an exhaustive list."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "request reason"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Why a request was issued."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03, SA-22. The individuals follow AM22's examples of remote assistance (a new path around road construction; classifying an object in the lane) and the takeover request of event-based remote driving. Not an exhaustive list."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "request type"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "What a vehicle asks the remote operator for."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EN95b" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "LV21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MZ25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-25. The measures often do not agree with each other, probes can change where operators look, and gaze is affected by 'look but not see' (MZ25), so each piece of evidence has a reliability."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SA evidence"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A recorded observation from which an operator's perception of an element is inferred."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EN95a" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "LV21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-22 (static), used by SA-13 (lapses) and SA-23 (sufficiency). For decision-support SA, a requirement may be limited to one request type (forRequestType), and it applies only to the elements the request concerns, where the request names any (concernsElement): what O must know depends on what V asks. Design-time knowledge, e.g. from a task analysis. The interval should reflect how fast elements of the type change; no source gives values."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SA requirement"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SARequirement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A requirement that an operator who needs a given SA type has perceived every situation element of a given type in the vehicle's scene, and rechecked it within a recheck interval. The recheck interval is the value, as qudt:numericValue with qudt:unit unit:SEC."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EN95a" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TANG26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-21. TANG26: remote driving relies on real-time, low-level information, remote assistance on high-level, synthesized information to support decisions. Supervisory SA follows AM22's remote monitoring."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SA type"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The kind of situation awareness a mode of operation requires."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SelfReportEvidence
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SelfReportEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SelfReportEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SelfReportEvidence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MZ25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SelfReportEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-25. A rating of SA as a whole, such as SART, is not evidence for one element."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SelfReportEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "self-report evidence"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SelfReportEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "SA evidence from the operator's own statement that they noticed the element, e.g. a verbal report during the drive."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFrame
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFrame> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFrame> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFrame> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-08. sosa:resultTime is the capture time at the vehicle and sosa:madeBySensor the sensor. The sensed time, when the depicted state of the world held, is the capture time minus the sensor's capture delay."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFrame> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sensor frame"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFrame> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One captured output of a vehicle sensor (camera image, lidar sweep) sent to the remote station."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorOverlay
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorOverlay> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorOverlay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InformationChannel> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorOverlay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-15."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorOverlay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sensor overlay"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorOverlay> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An information channel that draws sensor or perception data, such as detected objects or a predicted path, over the camera views."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SituationElement
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SituationElement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SituationElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-07. Interface. A.U.T.O. Traffic_Entity is a subclass (ROVO-core). This module never describes the element itself, only the operator's perception of it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SituationElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "situation element"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SituationElement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Something in the vehicle's situation that the operator may perceive: a road user, an object, an event or a state of the vehicle."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverReason
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverReason> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. Records the event that called for an event-based remote drive when there is no Request. The individuals are the two cases of a takeover from an on-board driver; no source states them, they follow from the context rule of event-based remote driving. Not an exhaustive list."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "takeover reason"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverReason> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Why a remote operator took over from an on-board driver, where no request from the vehicle started the engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TimeOnTaskLimit
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TimeOnTaskLimit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TimeOnTaskLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TimeOnTaskLimit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HA24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TimeOnTaskLimit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TimeOnTaskLimit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TANG26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TimeOnTaskLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-12. A break is any time without an engagement, including time fallback-ready, so breaks follow from the engagements and need no class of their own. Exact rules: (1) a break is a period of at least the minimum break length in which the operator has no open engagement with any vehicle, in any mode; (2) time on task is the sum of the durations of the operator's engagements in a remote driving mode (isRemoteDrivingMode true) since the end of the last break; (3) time in remote monitoring or remote assistance is neither: it adds nothing to time on task and is not a break, so it does not reset the count; (4) the limit and the minimum break length that apply are those of the mode of the operator's current remote driving engagement or, if the operator is not driving now, of the most recent one; a limit stated for the broader mode holds where the mode has none of its own. Both limit types are therefore stated for remote driving modes only (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl). HA24: most professional remote drivers never drove more than 2 h at a time, 1 h preferred."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TimeOnTaskLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "time-on-task limit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TimeOnTaskLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The longest time an operator may drive remotely in a mode without a break of at least the minimum break length. Value as qudt:numericValue with qudt:unit unit:MIN."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConfiguredLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HS88" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-18, SA-24. Scoped by appliesToMode, or by appliesToFallbackReady for the fallback-ready state, which has no mode. SA-24: workload is measured in the mode the operator is in and says nothing certain about another mode, so it is tested against the band of the current mode only; an operator outside that band, overloaded or underloaded, is not given a remote driving mode, and the other modes stay."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "workload band"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadBand> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The acceptable workload range in a mode, or while fallback-ready. Below the lower bound is underload, above the upper bound overload."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadEstimate
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadEstimate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadEstimate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadEstimate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HS88" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadEstimate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadEstimate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadEstimate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-18, SA-20. E.g. a NASA-TLX score (HS88) or a physiological index."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadEstimate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "workload estimate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WorkloadEstimate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An observation of the operator's workload: sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest the operator, sosa:observedProperty ROVO-op:Workload, sosa:hasSimpleResult the value, sosa:resultTime the time, onScale the scale."@en .
