# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AccelerationCue
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AccelerationCue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AccelerationCue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AccelerationCue> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ZH24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AccelerationCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-16. ZH24: remote drivers 'may have difficulty perceiving the acceleration and motion states of the vehicle when relying solely on video information'."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AccelerationCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "acceleration cue"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AccelerationCue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The forces a driver's body feels when the vehicle accelerates, brakes or corners."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AmbientSound
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AmbientSound> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AmbientSound> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AmbientSound> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AmbientSound> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AmbientSound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-16. TL22 and WO25 report the missing audio channel as a problem for remote operators."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AmbientSound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ambient sound"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#AmbientSound> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Sound from the vehicle's surroundings, such as traffic, people or machines."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConstructionSite
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConstructionSite> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConstructionSite> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConstructionSite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-06."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConstructionSite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "construction site"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ConstructionSite> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A site where construction work is carried out, closed to public traffic."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#broaderMode> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationalSA> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationalSA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "BR26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "SHI26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "STVF" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01. Term from SHI26. What starts the remote drive, not its duration, decides the context: a vehicle without an ADS that is remotely driven for a whole trip, even a short move on a site, is in continuous remote driving. Often lasts hours (group D). Responds to no request (SA-03)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "continuous remote driving"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ContinuousRemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Remote driving in which the remote operator is the vehicle's driver for the whole trip, however short, performing the whole DDT, possibly in a vehicle without an automated driving system."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CueInterpretationTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CueInterpretationTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionMakingTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionMakingTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionSupportSA
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionSupportSA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionSupportSA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionSupportSA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-21, SA-22. Required by remote assistance; the elements are those the request concerns, where it names any (concernsElement)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionSupportSA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "decision-support SA"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionSupportSA> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Selective awareness of the specific elements needed to answer a request from the system; not full SA of the scenario."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Distraction
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Distraction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Distraction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Distraction> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HA24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Distraction> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Distraction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-19. ME24; HA24 reports distraction in the remote operation office."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Distraction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "distraction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Distraction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The operator's attention being drawn away from the operation task."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EngineSound
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EngineSound> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EngineSound> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EngineSound> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ZH24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EngineSound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-16. ZH24 names the engine sound among the cues through which speed is perceived."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EngineSound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "engine sound"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EngineSound> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sound of the vehicle's engine or drive, which tells a driver about speed and load."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#broaderMode> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationalSA> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "SHI26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WF25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01, SA-03. SHI26 introduce the term for automated vehicles that call an operator in; ROVO-op also applies it to a takeover from remote monitoring and to a vehicle without an ADS taken over from its on-board driver (takenOverFrom). Not called an intervention, since WF25 use remote intervention for acting on the vehicle without driving it, such as starting a safe stop."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "event-based remote driving"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#EventBasedRemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Remote driving that an event calls for while something else drives the vehicle, either its ADS or an on-board driver. The operator takes over on the vehicle's takeover request, from remote monitoring when the operator sees the need, or from the on-board driver, usually for a limited time, and then hands back or ends the engagement."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Fatigue
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Fatigue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Fatigue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Fatigue> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HA24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Fatigue> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Fatigue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-19. HA24: fatigue clearly higher than in-vehicle driving; ME24."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Fatigue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fatigue"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Fatigue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A state of tiredness that lowers the operator's alertness and performance."@en .
