<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MiningSite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mining site"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MiningSite> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A surface or underground mine."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionSickness
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionSickness> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionSickness> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Impairment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionSickness> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HA24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionSickness> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionSickness> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionSickness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-19. HA24, ME24; TL22: operators felt nauseous and dizzy after 15 minutes."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionSickness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "motion sickness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#MotionSickness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Nausea, dizziness or similar discomfort that the operator gets from watching the vehicle's motion at the station."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObjectClassificationRequest
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObjectClassificationRequest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObjectClassificationRequest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObjectClassificationRequest> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObjectClassificationRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03, SA-22. AM22's example: an object in the lane is identified as an empty bag that can be driven through."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObjectClassificationRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "object classification request"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObjectClassificationRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A request that the remote operator say what an object is that the vehicle cannot classify."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObservationTask
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObservationTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverAsked
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverAsked> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverAsked> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverReason> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverAsked> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverAsked> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "on-board driver asked"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverAsked> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The on-board driver asked the remote operator to take over."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverUnableToDrive
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverUnableToDrive> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverUnableToDrive> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverReason> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverUnableToDrive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03, LK-10. The driver then has ableToTakeOver false, so control cannot be handed back."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverUnableToDrive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "on-board driver unable to drive"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OnBoardDriverUnableToDrive> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The on-board driver can no longer drive, e.g. through illness or fatigue, as the driver reports or a driver monitoring system detects."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationalSA
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationalSA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationalSA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-21, SA-22. Required by remote driving."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationalSA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "operational SA"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationalSA> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Continuous awareness of all relevant elements, to carry out the DDT."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OtherAssistanceRequest
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OtherAssistanceRequest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OtherAssistanceRequest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OtherAssistanceRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. Keeps the list open: the request types are examples, not an exhaustive list."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OtherAssistanceRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "other assistance request"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OtherAssistanceRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A request for remote assistance of a kind that no other request type covers."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PathRequest
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PathRequest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PathRequest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PathRequest> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PathRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03, SA-22. AM22's example: the remote assistant provides a new pathway around road construction, which the ADS executes."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PathRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "path request"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PathRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A request that the remote operator provide a path for the vehicle, or authorize one it proposes."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PedalFeel
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PedalFeel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PedalFeel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PedalFeel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PedalFeel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-16. TL22 reports the missing haptic channel as a problem for remote operators."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PedalFeel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pedal feel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PedalFeel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The resistance and travel a driver feels in the brake and accelerator pedals."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionError
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionError> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionError> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionError> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionError> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. MU21, citing California DMV 2019."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionError> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "perception error"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PerceptionError> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The vehicle's perception has misread the scene or cannot interpret it reliably."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PlanFailure
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PlanFailure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PlanFailure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PlanFailure> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PlanFailure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. MU21, citing Scholtz et al. 2004."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PlanFailure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "plan failure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PlanFailure> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The vehicle's planning finds no way to proceed in the situation."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Port
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Port> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Port> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Port> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-06."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Port> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "port"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Port> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A port terminal, or a logistics yard like one, closed to public traffic."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PublicRoad
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PublicRoad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PublicRoad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PublicRoad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HN25b" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PublicRoad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "STVF" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PublicRoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-06. The environment of StVFernLV and of HN25b's remote driving data."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PublicRoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "public road"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#PublicRoad> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Roads open to public traffic, which the vehicle shares with other road users."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#modeIncludesTask> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#CueInterpretationTask> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#modeIncludesTask> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionMakingTask> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#DecisionSupportSA> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "BSI1886" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "J3016" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01, SA-03. The ADS keeps performing the DDT. While it waits for the answer to a request it cannot go on by itself (ROVO-link:adsAbleToDrive)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "remote assistance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteAssistance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Remote operation in which the operator advises an ADS-equipped vehicle that is within its ODD but encounters a situation it cannot manage: the operator interprets cues and answers the vehicle's requests, without performing any part of the DDT."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationalSA> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "BSI1886" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "J3016" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01. AM22's remote driving mode: SAE Levels 0-2, where the operator is present and active at all times, and the DDT fallback of Level 3 and above. Engagements use one of its two narrower modes, event-based or continuous remote driving, which are told apart by what starts the remote drive, not by SAE level or duration."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "remote driving"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteDriving> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Remote operation in which the operator manually controls the vehicle by throttling, braking and steering, and is fully responsible for OEDR."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperationMode> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#modeIncludesTask> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#ObservationTask> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#requiresSAType> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SupervisorySA> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SupervisorySA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#isRemoteDrivingMode> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "BSI1886" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "SHI26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-01. SHI26 do not count monitoring as a separate form of remote operation, because it needs a defined objective. ROVO-op keeps it as a mode and gives it that objective through its SA requirement: keeping supervisory SA, i.e. noticing when the operator must step in (SA-21, SA-22)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "remote monitoring"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RemoteMonitoring> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Remote operation in which the operator only observes the vehicle and its situation, e.g. its task status or system diagnostics, without influencing the DDT. The operator can switch to remote assistance or remote driving."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFailure
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFailure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFailure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFailure> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFailure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. MU21, citing California DMV 2019."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFailure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sensor failure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SensorFailure> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A sensor of the vehicle has failed or delivers no usable data."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SpeedSense
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SpeedSense> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SpeedSense> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SpeedSense> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ZH24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SpeedSense> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-16. ZH24: speed 'is perceived through auditory and tactile cues such as the vehicle's engine sound and vibrations', and through the changing view of the surroundings."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SpeedSense> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "speed sense"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SpeedSense> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A driver's impression of how fast the vehicle is moving, from the flow of the surroundings, sound and vibration."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SupervisorySA
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SupervisorySA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SAType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SupervisorySA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-21, SA-22. Required by remote monitoring."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SupervisorySA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "supervisory SA"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#SupervisorySA> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Awareness of relevant changes in the driving environment relative to the driving system's capabilities, to judge whether the operator must step in by switching to remote assistance or remote driving."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverRequest
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverRequest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverRequest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestType> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverRequest> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverRequest> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "TL22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. Answered by an event-based remote driving engagement. Closely matches J3016's request to intervene (ROVO-core)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "takeover request"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#TakeoverRequest> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A request that the remote operator take over driving the vehicle."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnclassifiableObject
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnclassifiableObject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnclassifiableObject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnclassifiableObject> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "AM22" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnclassifiableObject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnclassifiableObject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "unclassifiable object"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnclassifiableObject> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The vehicle has detected an object that it cannot classify."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnspecifiedReason
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnspecifiedReason> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnspecifiedReason> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#RequestReason> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnspecifiedReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-03. Used so that every request has a reason value (ROVO-op-shapes.ttl)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnspecifiedReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "unspecified reason"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#UnspecifiedReason> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "No reason was given for the request."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#VestibularCue
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#VestibularCue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#VestibularCue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#VestibularCue> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO26" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#VestibularCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-16. WO26 relates vestibular feedback to presence and spatial awareness in remote driving."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#VestibularCue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "vestibular cue"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#VestibularCue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sense of the vehicle's motion and of one's own orientation that the balance organs give a driver in the vehicle."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Warehouse
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Warehouse> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Warehouse> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#OperatingEnvironment> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Warehouse> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Warehouse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-06. WO25 studied remotely controlled forklifts in a cold storage warehouse."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Warehouse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "warehouse"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Warehouse> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The inside of a warehouse or a similar storage site, e.g. where forklifts handle pallets."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WarningSound
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WarningSound> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WarningSound> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/rovo/op#InVehicleCue> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WarningSound> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "WO25" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WarningSound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-16. WO25: operators missed audio 'particularly to detect hazards, for example through honking or shouting'."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WarningSound> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "warning sound"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#WarningSound> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A sound meant to warn, such as a horn, a siren or a shout."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Workload
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Workload> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Workload> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Workload> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HS88" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Workload> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ME24" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Workload> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "MU21" .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Workload> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SA-18, SA-20. The property a WorkloadEstimate observes (sosa:observedProperty), as an Impairment is the property an ImpairmentObservation observes, so that every operator observation says what it is about. The measure and its range are given by the scale of the estimate (onScale), e.g. NASA-TLX (HS88). An estimate without sosa:observedProperty is still read as workload; the shapes report it as a warning."@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Workload> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "workload"@en .
<https://w3id.org/rovo/op#Workload> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The mental and physical demand that the operation places on the operator."@en .
